   "speech": "On returning, however, the servant reported that the visitor, a very sickly-looking man, had shown an irritable and stubborn insistence. Roumier laid aside a pale photograph of blossoming morning clouds and crossed to the writing desk where he received his visitors. Having given a sign to admit the stranger, he saw a man of vulgar appearance, of the market-place rogue type, dressed without regard to fashion and of doubtful tidiness; he was short of stature but dreadfully thin, which served him in place of high heels. A dull suffering flickered in his sunken eyes; his forehead was high, but hidden by strands of black hair forgotten by the comb; the nervousness of an educated man and the coarsening of life’s hard school were mingled in that face, which numbered, perhaps, a little over thirty years.",
